  "slug": "structure-biological-process-8512",
  "summary": "Pangenome-era resources now standardize repeat annotation and gene-family membership across genome panels, exposing diversity single-genome analyses miss.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reference resources that move beyond a single genome or a single data type toward panel-level, consistently annotated representations. WheatPanRef builds a linear pan-reference for wheat from reconciled Chinese Spring assemblies plus non-CS sequences from 37 accessions. Earl Grey ParTEA similarly builds a shared non-redundant transposable element library across genome panels to enable consistent comparative TE annotation. The cereal pangene atlas reports pangene membership rising 59-264% over single-genome analyses, indicating diversity hidden from individual references. tModBase v2.0 and PmiREN3.0 extend curated encyclopedic coverage to tRNA modifications and plant microRNAs, both incorporating AI-assisted access. What is new here is explicit reconciliation of diversity across panels rather than per-genome annotation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
